WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:05.380
Hey youtubers it's charlie and this week was
another double episode of Korra.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:07.170
So this video is going to be for Episodes
5 and 6.

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:11.580
The first one was the conclusion of the Beifong
Metal Bending Clan story and the second episode

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.950
was the beginning of a new Airbender arc up
at the Northern Temple.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.950
Who else almost threw up a little when they
revealed the final fate of the Earth King's

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.150
bear Bosco.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:23.250
I'm not a member of PETA or anything either
but something about Sky Bison jackets makes

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.320
me so angry.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:27.660
Hello new people, if you're just finding me
for the first time I do Weekly Korra videos.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.920
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.790
I'm also doing a special Comic Con giveaway
I'll explain at the end of this video.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:36.600
So since this video is for two episodes I'm
going to do top 10 WTF moments and then I'll

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:37.600
do my review.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.860
Careful for spoilers if you haven't seen them
yet.

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:43.730
I'll wait just a sec....Okay, here we go.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:46.120
Number 10 - Beifong Acupuncture

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:49.080
This was the climax of the Beifong v Beifong
episode.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:53.960
I was fairly satisfied with the way they explained
Lin's hatred of Suyin even if they skipped

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:54.960
a lot of things.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.000
Like Toph retiring and Lin never agreeing
to meet up with her again.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.400
It sounds like Toph was pretty active in everyone's
lives up till the events on Legend Of Korra.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:07.409
She was around while Opal was growing up,
and I know a lot of you are still confused.

00:01:07.409 --> 00:01:11.399
But she's not dead, Toph is just listed as
whereabouts unknown.

00:01:11.399 --> 00:01:13.610
There's no promise that she'll be back this
year.

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:16.159
Maybe in book 4 or maybe just in the comics.

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:19.380
But, Number 9 - Bolin versus Metalbending

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.590
It was awesome to see Korra pick up so fast.

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:26.049
I don't know that I believe she's the first
avatar to ever metal bend.

00:01:26.049 --> 00:01:31.119
It's possible but does Suyin know the complete
history of the Avatar lineage?

00:01:31.119 --> 00:01:32.119
I don't think so.

00:01:32.119 --> 00:01:35.030
Bolin learning to do it will take longer,
but I feel like the language Suyin used is

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:37.320
teasing that he will learn eventually.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:41.869
This season is moving pretty fast, so I wouldn't
be surprised if it happened in the next one

00:01:41.869 --> 00:01:43.380
or two episodes.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:46.969
His path to learning Metal bending and overcoming
his self doubt is just like Opal's.

00:01:46.969 --> 00:01:50.590
So I think they'll both achieve their bending
goals at the same time.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:55.579
It would be really cool to see them do a combo
metal and airbend move in a battle.

00:01:55.579 --> 00:01:57.700
Like classic Fire Ferrets style combo attack.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:00.139
Moving on to Number 8 - Brand New Beifong

00:02:00.139 --> 00:02:02.509
It took me a minute to get used to the new
Lin.

00:02:02.509 --> 00:02:05.270
Beifong Kale Smoothie kind of made me hungry
too.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:08.369
She's not super hippy dippy or anything now,
she's just mellowed out.

00:02:08.369 --> 00:02:14.230
She reminds me of early Toph, punching her
problems away.

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:16.550
The thing that really threw me off was seeing
her smile.

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:17.550
And not in an ironic way.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:20.540
Did anyone else get a Joo Dee vibe from last
airbender.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:23.240
Like she was almost too pleasant when she
stepped out of her room.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:27.160
I don't think anything funky is going on,
she just took her grumpy pants off.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.540
Number 7 - Lin Versus Suyin Fight

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:33.950
I feel like they gave this match the same
emotional weight and brutality you'd see with

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:37.080
Aang and Firelord Ozai or Azula and Zuko.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.360
No one was pulling any punches.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:43.360
If they really wanted to hurt each other though,
they'd be exclusively metalbending.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:48.300
The kind of blunt force trauma damage big
rocks do is way harder to sneak on another

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:52.800
earth bender than a really unpredictable cable
strike or lead projectile.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:57.050
It was more like a good old fashioned street
brawl like you'd see in a classic western

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:58.050
movie.

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:01.640
Which is funny, because Bumi's Airbender posse
felt like it was straight out of an old John

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:02.640
Wayne movie.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:07.390
I did think it was really cool they let Opal,
the airbender be the calming force.

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:11.500
Airbending is all about peace and tranquility,
so of course the best mediators would be airbenders.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:16.630
I saw an interesting theory some of you guys
were talking about last week.

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:19.010
That Opal is secretly Lin's daughter.

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:23.220
I don't think that's the case, but I think
Aunt Lin will be a much bigger part of the

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:24.590
family going forward.

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:28.950
Number 6 - Bumi Tells Tenzin to Go All Full
Metal Jacket On the Recruits

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:33.160
I loved listening to JK Simmons do his best
Tenzin as R Lee Ermey impression.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:36.530
When really it's Meelo that's the crazy drill
sergeant.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:41.020
Even though Episode was all airbenders it
felt like Tenzin was the least important person.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:44.370
It was really all about the new airbenders
coming together

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:50.360
There was one thing he said that struck me
as possibly really important for the future.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:54.420
At the beginning of the Obstacle Course he
said the Key is to maintain your heaven and

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.880
earth connection.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:04:01.190
The Guru Laghima pendant got mentioned and
even though he just made a mental note about

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:05.910
it I'm wondering if they're teeing up Zaheer's
plot, about learning Laghima's secrets.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:09.800
Number 5 - Airbender Ninja Warrior Obstacle
Course

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:10.940
This was too much fun.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:15.240
I don't watch America Ninja Warrior a lot
but just the idea of an obstacle course sounds

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:16.240
awesome.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:19.709
And Meelo with the Watermelon gun and that
evil evil smile.

00:04:19.709 --> 00:04:22.909
I want a watermelon gun at my next party.

00:04:22.909 --> 00:04:27.960
I'm way too old for summer camp, but did any
of you ever do obstacle courses at camp?

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:31.919
I never had to do one as crazy as the airbender
course, but there were monkey bars that hung

00:04:31.919 --> 00:04:33.580
over a pool we had to get across.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:37.430
This all teed up the Jinora story.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:39.990
Number 4 - Jinora wants her Tattoos

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:44.990
her argument to Kai was that she has attained
mastery over airbending and the sub form.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:49.440
As well as a deep connection to the spirits,
but without the tattoos you're just a pretender.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:55.830
I heard it's a similar thing in Russian Prisons,
like there you're tattoos are supposed to

00:04:55.830 --> 00:05:00.060
tell your life story, so the more things you've
done, the more tattoos you have.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:05.360
So if you ran into someone without any, it
means they're a nobody, they're nothing because

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:07.110
they have no life story.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:12.169
Thematically there are a lot of cultures that
use markings as a way to denote mastery or

00:05:12.169 --> 00:05:13.169
maturity.

00:05:13.169 --> 00:05:16.199
Even though I think Jinora will be a full
on master by the end of this season, I don't

00:05:16.199 --> 00:05:18.380
think she'll get tattoos yet.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:22.710
Avatar Yanchen is the most notable female
master airbender I can think of.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:24.830
That's pretty much what a grown up Jinora
would look like.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:31.820
They don't completely shave their heads like
the men.

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:35.779
Number 3 - Team Zaheer Goes After Korra

00:05:35.779 --> 00:05:37.620
Lavabending escape for the win.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:42.499
I love how Zaheer used the Guru Pathik chakra
technique of going into that astral state

00:05:42.499 --> 00:05:46.150
of meditation where you can sense the energy
of other beings.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:47.870
He has clearly done his homework.

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:52.400
I think there are a couple scenarios he could
be going for.

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:58.809
Either he's trying to bring back Guru Laghima
somehow or energy bend himself into Korra's

00:05:58.809 --> 00:05:59.809
body.

00:05:59.809 --> 00:06:06.460
Or achieve some secret technique of Laghima
that we haven't seen yet.

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:11.491
The two part finale is called Enter the Void
and Venom of the Red Lotus, The Void talk

00:06:11.491 --> 00:06:15.820
just makes me think of the astral state when
Aang and Korra were learning to energy bend.

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:20.439
But now it sounds like they're heading for
the Metal Clan.

00:06:20.439 --> 00:06:23.770
Number 2 - Sky Bison Rescue

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:29.029
I loved watching Bumi rally the other airbenders
and that the Wild Sky Bison zoomed in to rescue

00:06:29.029 --> 00:06:30.029
the others.

00:06:30.029 --> 00:06:32.560
For a minute I thought that Jinora would get
captured by the Earth Queen again.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:37.590
Did anyone else feel like Bumi and Boom Joom
were a joke making fun of Han Solo and Chewbacca.

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:42.129
Like when the other bender called him on being
able to speak the same language as Boom Joom

00:06:42.129 --> 00:06:44.499
and he just waved his hand and trailed off.

00:06:44.499 --> 00:06:46.979
I feel like that's totally Han Solo and Chewie.

00:06:46.979 --> 00:06:51.190
I already had a feeling the wild sky bison
were going to be a big part of the plot.

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:56.280
My first theory before the end of the episode
was that Meelo would do his crazy animal whispering

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:58.729
trick and tame them all in like fifteen minutes.

00:06:58.729 --> 00:07:01.099
Let me know if you think he could actually
do that.

00:07:01.099 --> 00:07:03.990
It doesn't matter now, they're completely
pacified.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:07.479
Time for a sky bison tutorial episode.

00:07:07.479 --> 00:07:13.939
but my Number 1 WTF Moment - The Earth Queen
Ate Her Father's Pet Bear Bosco

00:07:13.939 --> 00:07:16.889
This made me a little upset.

00:07:16.889 --> 00:07:20.940
Because yes, it's supposed to be a joke, but
she's crazy enough to do something like that.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:23.999
And Sky Bison veal, that's enough to make
anyone go vegan.

00:07:23.999 --> 00:07:28.110
I only noticed it when they were kicking his
ass, but the leader who totally sounded like

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:29.110
Clancy Brown.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:32.349
The guy who played Long Feng in last airbender.

00:07:32.349 --> 00:07:34.699
He was wearing a sky bison pelt.

00:07:34.699 --> 00:07:39.110
Kai's takedown was probably intended to be
a Tenzin Kai moment of clarity, but I really

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:42.699
wanted Kai to go too far and stab him with
the glider stick.

00:07:42.699 --> 00:07:47.219
In defense of the episode, that would have
been totally out of character for an airbender.

00:07:47.219 --> 00:07:48.839
But it would have looked pretty cool.

00:07:48.839 --> 00:07:53.210
Kai is actually a really proficient bender,
I have a feeling he'll learn Jinora's spirit

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:55.479
bending technique by the end of this season.

00:07:55.479 --> 00:08:00.590
But let me know what your biggest WTF moment
was and do you think the Earth Queen really

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:01.590
ate Bosco?

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:05.619
It sounds like she totally did given how awful
she is and all the other exotic animals she

00:08:05.619 --> 00:08:06.619
eats.

00:08:06.619 --> 00:08:09.770
Overall I gave episode 6 a B plus and Episode
7 an A minus.

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:14.080
I just thought the airbender episode moved
the real plot forward.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:15.979
The Guru Laghima story along with Team Zaheer.

00:08:15.979 --> 00:08:19.099
They were like the connective tissue between
the arcs.

00:08:19.099 --> 00:08:24.349
And even though the episodes were from separate
two parters, I didn't feel disconnected.

00:08:24.349 --> 00:08:28.119
I can't wait to see Bolin Metalbend.

00:08:28.119 --> 00:08:38.800
He and Bumi are still the Korra Class Clowns,
but they both got some really good moments.

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:42.919
Bumi's speech was actually one of the better
Korra speeches I've heard this season.

00:08:42.919 --> 00:08:47.870
And then to pay off the Family of Aang bit
with him finally feeling like part of the

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:49.840
Air Nation was important.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:54.540
I'm interested to see if he ever does shave
his head.

00:08:54.540 --> 00:09:00.200
He's a long ways from getting his tattoos,
but for some reason I just can't picture him

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:01.200
bald.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:04.769
Speaking of Bald, a lot of people are commenting
on the similarities between Kai and Aang.

00:09:04.769 --> 00:09:10.630
I do think they share a lot of character DNA,
but I don't think Kai's backstory will overlap

00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:12.529
with the Avatar's.

00:09:12.529 --> 00:09:23.829
It is 
possible that Team Zaheer has some familial

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:28.890
connection to the main characters, I know
everyone wanted Zaheer and P'Li to be related

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:30.310
to Mako and Bolin.

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:35.579
But let me know what your craziest Team Zaheer
theories are and here's the details on my

00:09:35.579 --> 00:09:36.579
comic con giveaway.

00:09:36.579 --> 00:09:40.820
If you didn't see it earlier I'm giving away
a pabu plush doll.

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:42.829
This is in addition to the regular giveaway.

00:09:42.829 --> 00:09:45.690
So all you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment.

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:49.089
I'll be at comic con so I'll upload the Korra
Panel.

00:09:49.089 --> 00:09:50.279
That's going to be next friday.

00:09:50.279 --> 00:09:58.190
They're doing two more episodes so I'll try
to get a review out that night.

00:09:58.190 --> 00:09:59.230
But it might be Saturday morning.

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:00.880
There's a lot of stuff going down.

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:05.760
Right now click here to learn all about the
new Airbending Sub form and click here for

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:07.250
my episode 4 and 5 video.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:08.790
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:09.229
High Fives!

